# TCLS r1: SAVE must not stick on "SAVES WHEN STOPPED". The OTA path used to call seq_stop, which
# set seq.req_stop and was cleared only by engine_all_off; a later SAVE then waited forever. The
# host's `stop` command sets the same seq.req_stop (it deliberately does not all-off), so it stands
# in for the OTA-cancel path: after it, SAVE must save.
wait 300
stop
tap SAVE
wait 300
expect store_writes >0
